      "comment": "Traupman’s word, built on <span lang=\"la\">rēte</span>, a net, and declined like it: ablative <span lang=\"la\">interrēte</span> (Lewis &amp; Short gives <span lang=\"la\">rēte</span> as the commoner ablative of <span lang=\"la\">rēte</span>, beside <span lang=\"la\">rētī</span>). The adjective is <span lang=\"la\">interrētiālis</span> (see online, website); in talk <span lang=\"la\">rēte</span> alone will do."
